*List, Map and Bytes Operators* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

*Lists and Bytes:*
''+'' - Concatenate two lists or two bytes (see ''append(container, value)'')
''*'' - Repeat list or bytes by number
''-'' - Remove element at index

''container[index]'' - Access element at index (available for lists, bytes and strings)
''container[index] = value'' - Assign element at index in place (lists and bytes)

Indices are 1-based.

*Maps:*
''m[]'' - Empty map
''m["key": value, "key2": value2]'' - Map with key-value pairs

''+'' - Merge two maps (right-hand / incoming side wins on key conflict)
''-'' - Remove a key by string: ''map - "key"''

''map["key"]'' - Access value by key (runtime error if key not found)
''map["key"] = value'' - Set key to value in place

See ''chippy doc mutability'', ''chippy doc keys'' and ''chippy doc has''.
